# ExtensionFixes Core Rules

ExtensionFixes is a Chrome extension warning lookup + alternatives guide + migration safety knowledge base.

MUST:
- Keep the site static-first.
- Use Next.js App Router, TypeScript, and Tailwind.
- Use local data files under src/data.
- Preserve extensionfixes.com canonical URLs.
- Run npm run verify after meaningful changes.

SHOULD:
- Prefer GSC-query-driven content.
- Add at most 1-3 pages per batch.
- Avoid near-duplicate pages.
- Update internal links when adding pages.

NEVER:
- Do not add API routes.
- Do not add database, auth, or login.
- Do not add affiliate links.
- Do not add dark mode.
- Do not add Chrome Scanner without a separate RFC.
- Do not delete existing pages without approval.
